        {
          "name": "comment",
          "value": "<p><strong>PURPOSE</strong></p><p>The entry point of the Order Review process — fetches a single order from Salesforce and creates its record in the orders database so it can be tracked, reviewed, and approved through every stage of the workflow.</p><p><strong>WHAT THIS WORKFLOW DOES</strong></p><p>1. Fetch Order Details</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Connects to Salesforce and pulls the order along with its account, owner, and creator information using the supplied order_id.</p><p>2. Prepare the Data</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Reshapes the nested Salesforce response (Account, Owner, CreatedBy) into a clean, flat structure suitable for the orders table.</p><p>3. Stamp Initial Status</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Marks the new order with the status \"Processing\" so the system knows it has just entered the review flow.</p><p>4. Save to Database</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Inserts the prepared order row into the orders table, making it visible in the Order Review dashboard.</p><p><strong>OUTCOME</strong></p><ul><li>A new order appears in the dashboard with status \"Processing\", ready for the next step — validation.</li></ul>",
          "widget": "textarea_rich"
        }
      ],
      "engine": "scala,pyspark,polars,agent",
      "inputAnchors": [],
      "outputAnchors": [],
      "agentTool": false
    },
